References: <FiEwe9a7r2o.CiiODfcfAwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <FiEwe9a7r2o.YdJvJ-8nAwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/FiEwe9a7r2o/m/934hwkkoAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You just do something like this:

parameters{
…
vector[L-2] z;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[L] x;
  for (i in 1:41) x[i] <- z[i];
  for (i in 42:65) x[i] <- z[i-1];
  for (i in 67:100) x[i] <- z[i-2];
  x[41] <- 1;
  x[66] <- -1;
}

model {
  z ~ normal(0,1);
…
}

Or something like that.  I might be mangling the syntax, also this is a bit of an ugly way to do it, but you should get the general idea.
A

