>
> For debian you'd have have a set of packages, one per interface all
> depending on a stan-dev package as well as standard c++ compiler
> package.
>
> Python packages usually have names like python-pystan, and I think R
> as is similar.
>
> There's a lot of documentation on packaging at least for Debian, so
