> I would be interested in your opinions regarding the convergence of my current version. I still see that most of the times three chains behave very nicely and the fourth is a bit stubborn. However, maybe overall the mixing is OK and I should just run the chains a little longer? I attached some  convergence plots for some of the many parameters (which also show effective sample sizes). The chains were run for 50000 iterations (plus 5000) warm-up which takes about 15 hours.

I would not consider this mixing — you’re still running into some pathological
geometries.  Where are the divergences?

Incidentally, this is a good example of why we recommend running many chains!

> Furthermore, should I devote any special attention to the mixing and convergence of the __lp variable (plot also included)?

It can be a really sensitive diagnostics of poor mixing but such an interpretation
needs to be done carefully.

