If you do that, your posterior is undefined because it can't
be normalized.  Stan should fail and tell you that, but it
might just lead to very crazy (and easily diagnosable) samples.

You may find the manual chapter on problematic priors helpful --- there's
a simple example of the kinds of problems it'll cause.

- Bob

