Subject: Don't use hard constraints in priors unless you really have hard constraints
Message-ID: <CMF8pZ6WSZ4.YpZVBWZuAAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CMF8pZ6WSZ4.3Kg-p11MAAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <CMF8pZ6WSZ4.f4IfIYrQAQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <CMF8pZ6WSZ4.3Kg-p11MAAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
